        <p class="hackathon-kicker">Project overview <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> WebMCP</p>
        <h1 id="hackathon-title">{{ siteConfig.name }}</h1>
        <p class="hero-thesis">Give an agent a task.<br>Keep the work in view.</p>
        <p class="hero-description">A visual control center that lets people and agents observe a screen, act on a goal, and check what happened next.</p>
        <p class="hero-tagline">Structured browser tools. One shared task state.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="hackathon-action primary" href="/"><Play :size="16" aria-hidden="true" />Launch demo</a>
          <a class="hackathon-action" href="/webmcp">Explore WebMCP tools<ArrowRight :size="16" aria-hidden="true" /></a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-secondary">
          <a v-if="validRepository" :href="validRepository" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><GitBranch :size="15" aria-hidden="true" />Git repository<ArrowUpRight :size="14" aria-hidden="true" /></a>
          <span v-else>[REPOSITORY_URL] not configured</span>
          <a v-if="videoEmbed" :href="siteConfig.videoUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><Video :size="15" aria-hidden="true" />Watch demo<ArrowUpRight :size="14" aria-hidden="true" /></a>
          <a v-else href="#demo-video"><Video :size="15" aria-hidden="true" />Demo video pending</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-loop" aria-label="The browser Lab workflow">
        <div class="loop-heading"><span class="loop-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i></span><span>THE VISIBLE LOOP</span><span class="loop-mode">Browser Lab</span></div>
        <div class="loop-goal"><span>YOUR GOAL</span><p>Chop wood. If chopping stops, find another tree.</p></div>
        <div class="loop-operation"><Eye :size="20" aria-hidden="true" /><div><strong>Observe the frame</strong><code>desktop_observe</code></div><span class="loop-index">01</span></div>
        <span class="loop-connector" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="loop-operation"><SquareTerminal :size="20" aria-hidden="true" /><div><strong>Take a bounded action</strong><code>desktop_action</code></div><span class="loop-index">02</span></div>
        <span class="loop-connector" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="loop-operation"><Check :size="20" aria-hidden="true" /><div><strong>Check the visible result</strong><code>desktop_until</code></div><span class="loop-index">03</span></div>
        <div class="loop-return"><span aria-hidden="true">↳</span> If the condition changes, observe again.</div>
        <div class="loop-person"><ShieldCheck :size="17" aria-hidden="true" />The person can pause or stop.</div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="demo-availability"><span class="availability-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><p><strong>Try it now in the browser Lab.</strong> No bridge, API key, or account required. The Windows installer is paused pending Norton review. Real Windows input remains unverified for the updated release.</p><a href="/bridge-download-status.html">Release status<ArrowUpRight :size="14" aria-hidden="true" /></a></div>

    <nav class="hackathon-jumps" aria-label="Overview sections"><a href="#the-project">The project</a><a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a><a href="#feature-showcase">Features</a><a href="#demo-video">Demo video</a><a href="#submission">Submission</a><a href="#contribute">Contribute</a></nav>

    <section id="the-project" class="hackathon-section project-section" aria-labelledby="project-heading">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="hackathon-kicker">01 / The project</p><h2 id="project-heading">One click is rarely<br>the whole task.</h2></div>
      <div class="project-explanation"><p>Lense is for people who want to supervise a repeated visual task and developers building agents that work with visible applications. A script can click once. A useful task also needs to notice a stopped activity, inspect the new state, and decide whether to continue.</p><p>You choose a goal and a source. The task engine observes, acts, and checks the result. The preview, queue, and event history show the same work an agent sees through WebMCP.</p><p class="plain-boundary">The included pixel evaluator understands the Woodcutting Lab. Other applications need an external WebMCP agent or a provider adapter. Lense does not include a general desktop model or a RuneScape planner.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="hackathon-section why-section" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="hackathon-kicker">Why WebMCP fits</p><h2 id="why-heading">The agent can ask<br>the app directly.</h2><p>Visual evidence still matters. Guessing how to operate Lense does not need to.</p></div>
      <div class="shared-experience">
        <div><span class="experience-label">THE PERSON</span><h3>Chooses the scope</h3><p>Set the goal, duration, cadence, and limits. Select the screen or window. Review results, pause a task, export history, or stop control.</p></div>
        <div><span class="experience-label">THE AGENT</span><h3>Uses declared operations</h3><p>Discover tool names and schemas, capture a frame, send a bounded action, wait for an event, and receive a structured result.</p></div>
        <div class="shared-state-note"><GitBranch :size="20" aria-hidden="true" /><p><strong>They share Pinia state.</strong> A tool updates the same task and queue that Vue renders. Native access still requires the visible Pair button and separate Windows approval. Opening this page grants no access and starts no task.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="how-it-works" class="hackathon-section architecture-section" aria-labelledby="architecture-heading">
      <div class="section-top"><div><p class="hackathon-kicker">02 / How it works</p><h2 id="architecture-heading">A declared call becomes<br>a visible state change.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/webmcp">Inspect the contracts<ArrowRight :size="15" aria-hidden="true" /></a></div>
      <ol class="architecture-flow" aria-label="Request to result architecture"><li v-for="(step,index) in architectureSteps" :key="step.title"><span class="architecture-number">{{ String(index + 1).padStart(2,'0') }}</span><h3>{{ step.title }}</h3><p>{{ step.detail }}</p><ArrowRight v-if="index < architectureSteps.length-1" class="architecture-arrow" :size="17" aria-hidden="true" /></li></ol>
      <div class="architecture-foundation"><div><Code2 :size="18" aria-hidden="true" /><h3>Browser application</h3><p>Vue 3 + TypeScript, Pinia, and IndexedDB task history. Vite builds the static app hosted on Netlify.</p></div><div><Monitor :size="18" aria-hidden="true" /><h3>Adapters and native service</h3><p>DesktopAdapter separates the browser Lab from BridgeClient. The optional Rust / Axum bridge handles native capture, input, and visual watches on authenticated loopback connections.</p></div><div><ShieldCheck :size="18" aria-hidden="true" /><h3>Explicit control</h3><p>The local bridge owns desktop permissions. Task IDs and observation IDs reject stale actions. Pause cancels work; Stop revokes native access.</p></div></div>
      <details class="implementation-details"><summary>WebMCP implementation notes<Code2 :size="17" aria-hidden="true" /></summary><div class="implementation-grid"><div><h3>Imperative registration</h3><p>The application registers named tool definitions with <code>document.modelContext.registerTool</code> when available. The local <code>window.lense</code> registry provides a development fallback. Names such as <code>desktop_observe</code> describe one application capability.</p></div><div><h3>Schemas and results</h3><p>Canonical JSON Schemas define bounded inputs. Runtime handlers validate action fields, targets, limits, and task context. Tools return JSON-compatible results; observations also return image content. Read-only tools carry <code>readOnlyHint</code> annotations.</p></div><div><h3>State and lifecycle</h3><p>The existing application shell owns registration across Control, WebMCP, and Overview. Both the interface and tools call the control store. IndexedDB persists history; refresh does not restart tasks.</p></div><div><h3>Failures and evidence</h3><p>Errors return a code and message. A successful action with <code>observationError</code> means capture failed after input, so the caller must capture again without repeating the action. Unit and browser tests check contracts, cancellation, recovery, and visible state using mock native input.</p></div></div></details>
    </section>

    <section id="feature-showcase" class="hackathon-section" aria-labelledby="showcase-heading"><div class="section-top"><div><p class="hackathon-kicker">03 / What you can try</p><h2 id="showcase-heading">Small demonstrations.<br>Real application behavior.</h2></div><p class="section-side-note">Copy a prompt to a connected agent. Review the requested target and action before a desktop demonstration.</p></div><div class="feature-grid"><article v-for="(feature,index) in featureShowcase" :key="feature.title" class="feature-card"><span class="feature-number">{{ String(index+1).padStart(2,'0') }}</span><h3>{{ feature.title }}</h3><p class="feature-goal">{{ feature.goal }}</p><dl><dt>Person</dt><dd>{{ feature.human }}</dd><dt>Tools</dt><dd class="tool-chain">{{ feature.tools }}</dd><dt>Visible result</dt><dd>{{ feature.outcome }}</dd></dl><p v-if="feature.note" class="feature-note">{{ feature.note }}</p><details class="prompt-details"><summary>Demonstration prompt</summary><p>{{ feature.prompt }}</p></details><CopyButton :text="feature.prompt" label="Copy demo prompt" /></article></div></section>

    <section id="comparison" class="hackathon-section" aria-labelledby="comparison-heading"><div class="section-top"><div><p class="hackathon-kicker">04 / The difference</p><h2 id="comparison-heading">Less interface guessing.<br>More explicit results.</h2></div><p class="section-side-note">Qualitative comparisons of the same goals. No unmeasured speed or accuracy claims.</p></div><div class="comparison-list"><article v-for="comparison in comparisons" :key="comparison.title" class="comparison-card"><h3>{{ comparison.title }}</h3><div class="comparison-methods"><div><span>Manual workflow</span><p>{{ comparison.manual }}</p></div><div><span>Screenshot / DOM agent</span><p>{{ comparison.screenshot }}</p></div><div class="webmcp-method"><span>WebMCP workflow</span><p>{{ comparison.webmcp }}</p></div></div><div class="comparison-result"><p><strong>Experience.</strong> {{ comparison.improvement }}</p><p><strong>Reliability.</strong> {{ comparison.reliability }}</p></div></article></div></section>

    <section class="owner-note" aria-labelledby="owner-heading"><p class="hackathon-kicker">From the project owner</p><h2 id="owner-heading">What this foundation<br>lets me build next</h2><div><p>I want to describe a task once and see why the next action happened. With Lense, I can put task controls, screenshots, event waits, and recovery into one loop that both a person and an agent can inspect.</p><p>I can connect a different evaluator through the provider contract, add a service through an adapter, or add a tool without rebuilding the interface around it. The browser Lab lets me test that loop today. Reliable control of another application still depends on a working bridge, the selected target, and an agent that can interpret that application's screen.</p></div></section>

    <section id="demo-video" class="hackathon-section" aria-labelledby="video-heading"><div class="section-top"><div><p class="hackathon-kicker">05 / The demo</p><h2 id="video-heading">Two minutes, fifty seconds.<br>Follow the whole loop.</h2></div><span class="video-duration"><Video :size="16" aria-hidden="true" />2:50 recording plan</span></div><div class="video-frame"><iframe v-if="videoEmbed" :src="videoEmbed" title="Lense public WebMCP demo video" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe><div v-else class="video-placeholder"><span class="placeholder-play" aria-hidden="true"><Play :size="30" /></span><h3>The public demo video will appear here.</h3><p>The recording plan is ready. A public YouTube video with narration is still needed.</p><code>[YOUTUBE_URL]</code><a href="#recording-script" @click="openRecordingScript">Read the recording script<ArrowDown :size="15" aria-hidden="true" /></a></div></div><p class="video-note">The recording uses Woodcutting lab in the browser. It does not depend on the paused Windows installer. {{ demoSpokenWords }} spoken words, approximately {{ Math.round(demoSpokenWords / (170 / 60)) }} words per minute.</p>
      <details id="recording-script" class="recording-script"><summary><span>Complete narrated recording script<small>Screen actions, exact narration, tools, and visible results</small></span><Video :size="19" aria-hidden="true" /></summary><div class="script-intro"><p>Prepare a fresh Lab session with no active task or queued items. Use a WebMCP-capable browser and a connected agent. If recording the local fallback instead, label it as the local registry demonstration. Record real results and keep the primary 70-second workflow uninterrupted.</p><CopyButton :text="scriptText" label="Copy full script" /><a class="inline-link" href="/docs/demo-video-script.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Markdown script<ExternalLink :size="14" aria-hidden="true" /></a></div><ol class="script-segments"><li v-for="segment in demoSegments" :key="segment.time"><div class="segment-title"><time>{{ segment.time }}</time><h3>{{ segment.title }}</h3></div><dl><dt>Screen action</dt><dd>{{ segment.action }}</dd><dt>Exact narration</dt><dd class="narration">{{ segment.narration }}</dd><dt>WebMCP tools</dt><dd class="segment-tools">{{ segment.tools }}</dd><dt>Expected visible result</dt><dd>{{ segment.result }}</dd></dl></li></ol><details class="script-arguments"><summary>Primary task arguments</summary><pre>{{ JSON.stringify(demoTaskArguments,null,2) }}</pre><CopyButton :text="JSON.stringify(demoTaskArguments,null,2)" label="Copy task arguments" /><p>For each queued example, use operation <code>enqueue</code> and change <code>durationMs</code> to <code>6000</code>. Review the queue before calling <code>run-queue</code>.</p></details></details>
    </section>

    <section id="submission" class="hackathon-section submission-section" aria-labelledby="submission-heading"><div class="section-top"><div><p class="hackathon-kicker">06 / Submission readiness</p><h2 id="submission-heading">What is ready.<br>What still needs an owner.</h2></div><ListChecks :size="28" aria-hidden="true" /></div><p class="submission-context">This is a project readiness checklist, not a record of a submitted entry. Event eligibility and final submission have not been verified. URLs are configured once in <code>src/site/site-config.json</code>.</p><ul class="submission-checklist"><li v-for="item in submissionChecklist" :key="item.key"><Check v-if="checklistState(item.key).state === 'available'" :size="18" aria-hidden="true" /><CircleHelp v-else :size="18" aria-hidden="true" /><div><h3>{{ item.title }}</h3><p>{{ item.detail }}</p></div><span class="checklist-status" :class="checklistState(item.key).state">{{ checklistState(item.key).label }}</span></li></ul><div class="submission-links"><a v-if="siteConfig.liveUrl && !siteConfig.liveUrl.startsWith('[')" :href="siteConfig.liveUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Live demo<ArrowUpRight :size="15" aria-hidden="true" /></a><a v-if="validRepository" :href="validRepository" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source repository<ArrowUpRight :size="15" aria-hidden="true" /></a><a v-if="siteConfig.license" href="/license.txt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{ siteConfig.license }} license<ArrowUpRight :size="15" aria-hidden="true" /></a></div></section>

    <section id="contribute" class="hackathon-section" aria-labelledby="contribute-heading"><div class="section-top"><div><p class="hackathon-kicker">07 / Extend the project</p><h2 id="contribute-heading">Keep one contract<br>for people and agents.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/webmcp">Tool documentation<ArrowRight :size="15" aria-hidden="true" /></a></div><ol class="contribution-list"><li v-for="(step,index) in contributionSteps" :key="step.title"><span class="contribution-number">{{ String(index+1).padStart(2,'0') }}</span><div><h3>{{ step.title }}</h3><p>{{ step.detail }}</p><code class="contribution-path">{{ step.path }}</code></div></li></ol><details class="development-commands"><summary>Existing development and verification commands<SquareTerminal :size="18" aria-hidden="true" /></summary><pre>pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm dev
pnpm test
pnpm test:release
pnpm build
pnpm exec playwright install chromium
pnpm test:e2e</pre><p>The project uses <code>pnpm verify</code> to run the combined web checks. Bridge source tests use <code>cargo test --manifest-path bridge/Cargo.toml</code>. See the README for Windows tooling and the current release blocker.</p><pre>npx netlify-cli deploy --prod --dir dist --no-build</pre><p>Deploy from the already linked project after a successful build. Netlify authentication and access to the existing site are required.</p></details></section>

    <footer class="hackathon-footer"><div><span class="hackathon-kicker">Start with the browser Lab</span><h2>See the next action.<br>Understand the result.</h2></div><a class="hackathon-action primary" href="/">Launch demo<ArrowRight :size="17" aria-hidden="true" /></a></footer>
  </article>
